Docker Interview Questions and Answers (.NET 8 + AWS Project)

Answers are in spoken style and tied to this architecture: ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8), React.js / ASP.NET Core MVC, AWS EC2, ECR, RDS SQL Server, and Jenkins.

1. Docker Fundamentals

Q1. What is Docker?
Docker is a containerization platform that packages an application with its dependencies, libraries, configuration, and runtime into a single unit called an image. In my project, we built a Docker image of our .NET 8 Web API and ran it as a container on EC2 instead of deploying directly to the server. The main advantage is that the app behaves the same in development, testing, staging, and production.

Q2. What is a Docker container?
A container is a running instance of a Docker image. When we run our .NET 8 API image, Docker creates a container with the runtime and dependencies the app needs. We can run multiple containers from the same image.

Q3. Image vs container?

Docker image	Docker container
A blueprint	A running instance
Generally immutable	Has a writable container layer
Created using a Dockerfile	Created from an image
Can be stored in ECR	Runs on EC2 or another container host

Spoken: “An image is like a template, and a container is the actual running application created from it. We build one API image and run many containers from it.”

Q4. What is a Dockerfile?
A text file with instructions to build an image: base SDK image, working directory, source code, NuGet restore, build and publish, runtime image, and startup command.

dockerfile
FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/sdk:8.0 AS build
WORKDIR /src
COPY . .
RUN dotnet restore
RUN dotnet publish -c Release -o /app/publish

FROM mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/aspnet:8.0
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=build /app/publish .
EXPOSE 8080
ENTRYPOINT ["dotnet", "MyApi.dll"]

Q5. Docker vs virtual machine?
A VM has its own guest OS, while containers share the host OS kernel. VMs are heavier and need more resources. Containers are lightweight, start faster, and make deployment easier. We used containers to run our .NET apps on EC2.

Q6. Main advantages of Docker?
Portability, lightweight deployment, scalability, isolation, consistency, and faster delivery. In our project, we packaged frontend and backend separately and deployed them consistently across environments.

2. Frequently Asked Docker Commands

